module

public import Feec.Models.Torus.DeRham
public import Feec.HilbertComplex.CompressCompact

/-!
# The de Rham complex of the cube `(0, ½)ⁿ` by the method of images: relative and absolute classes

The cube `Q = (0, ½)ⁿ` (`Feec.Models.Cube.Geometry.Q`) is a fundamental domain of the group
`(ℤ/2)ⁿ` generated by the reflections `R_j : x_j ↦ -x_j` of the torus `𝕋ⁿ = ℝⁿ/ℤⁿ`. The
pull-back of a `k`-form `ω = Σ_s ω_s dx_s` by `R_j` is `R_j^* ω = Σ_s ε_j(s) (ω_s ∘ R_j) dx_s`,
`ε_j(s) = -1` if `j ∈ s` and `1` otherwise, and it commutes with `d`. On the Fourier side of the
torus de Rham complex (`Feec.Models.Torus.DeRham.window`) it acts by `n ↦ flip_j n` on the
frequencies and by the sign `ε_j(s)` on the coefficients (`reflForm`); the Koszul symbol
satisfies `(R_j ξ) ∧ R_j^* v = R_j^*(ξ ∧ v)` (`koszulDeg_reflForm`). Two classes of forms on the
cube arise as fixed complexes (the method of images, `Feec.HilbertComplex.Action.fixedComplex`):

* **relative** (`relative d`, fixed by `-R_j^*` for every `j`): `ω_s` is odd in `x_j` for
  `j ∉ s` and even for `j ∈ s`, so the tangential components vanish on the faces `x_j ∈ {0, ½}`
  (**tangential trace zero**, `H̊Λ`);
* **absolute** (`absolute d`, fixed by `R_j^*`): the opposite parities, so the normal components
  vanish (**normal trace zero**, `H*̊Λ`).

The Hilbert complexes are the compressions of the torus complex; this file proves, in every
dimension and degree:

* **the compactness property** (`hasCompactProperty`; Rellich and Gaffney on cubes in this
  model), from the torus (`Feec.Models.Torus.DeRham.window_hasCompactProperty`) by
  `Feec.HilbertComplex.Action.hasCompactProperty_fixedComplex`;
* closed range of `d` and of `d†` in every degree (`closedRangeAt`, `dual_closedRangeAt`), with
  the **Poincaré inequality** `‖u‖ ≤ (2π)⁻¹ ‖d u‖` on `D(d) ∩ N(d)ᗮ` (`norm_le_of_mem_orthogonal`);
* **the harmonic forms**: only the zero Fourier mode is harmonic on the torus, and the parities
  kill every constant coefficient except `dx_1 ∧ ⋯ ∧ dx_n` (relative) or `1` (absolute):
  `relative_harmonic_eq_bot` (degrees `< n`), `finrank_relative_harmonic_top` (`= 1` in degree
  `n`), `absolute_harmonic_eq_bot` (degrees `> 0`), `finrank_absolute_harmonic_zero` (`= 1` in
  degree `0`: the constants), and their duality `k ↔ n - k`
  (`finrank_relative_harmonic_eq_absolute`);
* **a complete set of eigenvectors** for the Hodge wave group (`eigenDense`), from the compact
  resolvent.
* **the Hodge star exchanges the two classes**: `dx_s ↦ dx_{sᶜ}` (the Hodge star up to the sign
  of each coefficient) maps the `k`-forms of one class unitarily onto the `(n - k)`-forms of the
  other (`hodgeStar`, `starLp_mem_fixed_iff`), and harmonic forms onto harmonic forms
  (`hodgeStar_mem_harmonic_iff`, `harmonicHodgeStar`, `finrank_harmonic_eq_rev`).

**Scope of the model.** The two classes are *defined* as fixed complexes of the parity action on
the Fourier coefficients of the torus complex, with complex coefficients (the Fourier side of the
torus complex). Their identification with the boundary-condition spaces `H̊Λ(Q)` (relative class)
and `HΛ(Q)` (absolute class) of `Feec.Domain.DeRham` is proved in `Feec.Models.Cube.DeRhamIdent`
(`HQmin_eq_compress`, `HQmax_eq_compress`: the parity extension is a scaled isometry, inner
products times `2ⁿ`, and the parity classes are the complexifications of the forms on `Q`,
`mem_parity_fixed_iff`); the Poincaré inequality, compactness and harmonic forms of `HΛ(Q)` and
`H̊Λ(Q)` themselves follow in `Feec.Models.Cube.DeRhamIdentPoincare`.
The intertwining `⋆ d = ± d† ⋆` of the Hodge star with the differentials is not formalized; only
the unitary exchange of the spaces and of the harmonic forms is.

## Main definitions

* `reflFreq` (the reflection of `ℝᵈ` matching `Feec.Fourier.Torus.flipAt`, `freq_flipAt`),
  `reflSign`, `reflForm`, `parSign`; `symmetries`, `action`, `complex`, `relative`, `absolute`.
* `complForm`, `starLp`, `hodgeStar`, `harmonicHodgeStar` (the Hodge star up to sign).

## Main results

* `koszulDeg_reflForm`, `deRham_reflForm`, `mem_fixed_iff`, `mem_window_harmonic_iff`.
* **`hasCompactProperty`**, `closedRangeAt`, `dual_closedRangeAt`, **`norm_le_of_mem_orthogonal`**,
  **`eigenDense`**.
* **`relative_harmonic_eq_bot`**, **`finrank_relative_harmonic_top`**,
  **`absolute_harmonic_eq_bot`**, **`finrank_absolute_harmonic_zero`**,
  `finrank_relative_harmonic_eq_absolute`, `finrank_relative_harmonic_eq_absolute_rev`.
* **`starLp_mem_fixed_iff`**, **`hodgeStar_mem_harmonic_iff`**, `finrank_harmonic_eq_rev`.

## References

* [D. N. Arnold, R. S. Falk, R. Winther, *Finite element exterior calculus: from Hodge theory to numerical stability*][AFW2010],
  §4.3 (the compactness property of the de Rham complex, relative and absolute boundary
  conditions)
* [D. N. Arnold, *Finite Element Exterior Calculus*][Arnold2018], Ch. 6 (the de Rham complex with
  boundary conditions; harmonic forms)
* [D. N. Arnold, R. S. Falk, R. Winther, *Finite element exterior calculus, homological techniques, and applications*][AFW2006]
  (the Koszul complex)
* [V. Quenneville-Bélair, *A New Approach to Finite Element Simulations of General Relativity*][QuennevilleBelair2015],
  §4.2 (the compactness property), §4.10 (the cube by the method of images)

Bibliography: [references.bib](../../../docs/references.bib)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open scoped InnerProductSpace
open MeasureTheory LinearPMap Set Feec.Fourier Feec.Fourier.Exterior Finset

namespace Feec.Models.Cube.DeRham

open Feec.Models.Torus.DeRham (window windowSymbol window_hasCompactProperty window_cartan gap)
open Feec.Fourier.Torus (flipAt flipAt_apply flipAt_involutive flipAt_comm flipAt_zero
  flipAt_eq_zero_iff)

variable {d : Type*} [Fintype d] [LinearOrder d]

omit [Fintype d] [LinearOrder d] in
theorem coeFn_zero_count {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] (n : d → ℤ) :
    ((0 : Lp E 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) : (d → ℤ) → E) n = 0 :=
  Measure.ae_count_iff.1 (Lp.coeFn_zero E 2 _) n

omit [Fintype d] [LinearOrder d] in
theorem coeFn_smul_count {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℂ E] (a : ℂ)
    (f : Lp E 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) (n : d → ℤ) :
    ((a • f : Lp E 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) : (d → ℤ) → E) n = a • f n :=
  Measure.ae_count_iff.1 (Lp.coeFn_smul a f) n

/-! ### The reflections on the Fourier side -/

/-- The reflection `ξ ↦ (…, -ξ_j, …)` of the frequency space. -/
def reflFreq (j : d) (ξ : EuclideanSpace ℝ d) : EuclideanSpace ℝ d :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 fun a => if a = j then -ξ a else ξ a

omit [Fintype d] in
theorem reflFreq_apply (j : d) (ξ : EuclideanSpace ℝ d) (a : d) :
    reflFreq j ξ a = if a = j then -ξ a else ξ a := rfl

omit [Fintype d] in
theorem freq_flipAt (j : d) (n : d → ℤ) :
    Fourier.Torus.freq (flipAt j n) = reflFreq j (Fourier.Torus.freq n) := by
  ext a
  simp only [Fourier.Torus.freq_apply, flipAt_apply, reflFreq_apply]
  split_ifs <;> push_cast <;> ring

/-- The sign `ε_j(s)` of `R_j^* dx_s = ε_j(s) dx_s`: `-1` if `j ∈ s`, `1` otherwise. -/
def reflSign (j : d) (s : Finset d) : ℂ := if j ∈ s then -1 else 1

omit [Fintype d] in
theorem reflSign_mul_self (j : d) (s : Finset d) : reflSign j s * reflSign j s = 1 := by
  unfold reflSign; split_ifs <;> norm_num

omit [Fintype d] in
/-- `ε_j` of `s ∖ l` times the sign of `ξ_l` under `R_j` is `ε_j(s)`, for `l ∈ s`. -/
theorem reflSign_erase {j l : d} {s : Finset d} (hl : l ∈ s) :
    (if l = j then (-1 : ℂ) else 1) * reflSign j (s.erase l) = reflSign j s := by
  unfold reflSign
  by_cases h : l = j
  · subst h; simp [hl]
  · have : j ∈ s.erase l ↔ j ∈ s := by simp [Finset.mem_erase, Ne.symm h]
    simp [h, this]

/-- `R_j^*` on the coefficients of a `k`-form at one frequency. -/
def reflForm (j : d) (k : ℤ) : Form ℂ d k →L[ℂ] Form ℂ d k :=
  LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap
    { toFun := fun v => WithLp.toLp 2 fun t => reflSign j t.1 * v t
      map_add' := fun v w => by ext t; simp [mul_add]
      map_smul' := fun a v => by ext t; simp; ring }

theorem reflForm_apply (j : d) (k : ℤ) (v : Form ℂ d k) (t : {s : Finset d // (#s : ℤ) = k}) :
    reflForm j k v t = reflSign j t.1 * v t := rfl

theorem reflForm_reflForm (j : d) (k : ℤ) (v : Form ℂ d k) : reflForm j k (reflForm j k v) = v := by
  ext t; rw [reflForm_apply, reflForm_apply, ← mul_assoc, reflSign_mul_self, one_mul]

theorem reflForm_comm (j l : d) (k : ℤ) (v : Form ℂ d k) :
    reflForm j k (reflForm l k v) = reflForm l k (reflForm j k v) := by
  ext t; simp only [reflForm_apply]; ring

theorem inner_reflForm (j : d) (k : ℤ) (v w : Form ℂ d k) :
    ⟪reflForm j k v, reflForm j k w⟫_ℂ = ⟪v, w⟫_ℂ := by
  simp only [PiLp.inner_apply, reflForm_apply]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun t _ => ?_
  unfold reflSign; split_ifs <;> simp [RCLike.inner_apply]

/-- **The Koszul symbol is reflection-equivariant**: `κ_{R_j ξ} (R_j^* v) = R_j^* (κ_ξ v)`
(`R_j^*` is an algebra automorphism of `Λ` with `R_j^* ξ = R_j ξ`). -/
theorem koszulDeg_reflForm (j : d) (k : ℤ) (ξ : EuclideanSpace ℝ d) (v : Form ℂ d k) :
    koszulDeg k (reflFreq j ξ) (reflForm j k v) = reflForm j (k + 1) (koszulDeg k ξ v) := by
  ext u
  rw [reflForm_apply, koszulDeg_apply, koszulDeg_apply, res_apply, res_apply, koszul_apply,
    koszul_apply, Finset.mul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l hl => ?_
  have he : (ext k (reflForm j k v) : Lam ℂ d) (u.1.erase l) =
      reflSign j (u.1.erase l) * (ext k v : Lam ℂ d) (u.1.erase l) := by
    by_cases h : (#(u.1.erase l) : ℤ) = k
    · rw [ext_apply k _ h, ext_apply k _ h, reflForm_apply]
    · rw [ext_apply_of_ne k _ h, ext_apply_of_ne k _ h, mul_zero]
  rw [he, ← reflSign_erase hl, reflFreq_apply]
  split_ifs <;> push_cast <;> ring

/-- **The de Rham symbol is reflection-equivariant**, in every pair of degrees. -/
theorem deRham_reflForm (j : d) (p q : ℤ) (ξ : EuclideanSpace ℝ d) (v : Form ℂ d p) :
    (deRham d).m p q (reflFreq j ξ) (reflForm j p v) = reflForm j q ((deRham d).m p q ξ v) := by
  by_cases h : p + 1 = q
  · subst h
    rw [deRham_m_succ, deRham_m_succ, _root_.smul_apply, _root_.smul_apply, koszulDeg_reflForm,
      _root_.map_smul]
  · have h0 : ∀ ξ, (deRham d).m p q ξ = 0 := fun ξ => by rw [(deRham d).shape p q h]; rfl
    rw [h0, h0]; simp

/-! ### The two parity classes -/

/-- The overall sign of the class: `-1` for the relative class (`ω = -R_j^* ω`), `1` for the
absolute class (`ω = R_j^* ω`). -/
def parSign (rel : Bool) : ℂ := if rel then -1 else 1

theorem parSign_mul_self (rel : Bool) : parSign rel * parSign rel = 1 := by
  cases rel <;> norm_num [parSign]

theorem conj_parSign_mul_self (rel : Bool) : (starRingEnd ℂ) (parSign rel) * parSign rel = 1 := by
  cases rel <;> norm_num [parSign]

variable (d) in
/-- **The reflections of the cube**, as fibre symmetries of the torus de Rham window:
`n ↦ flip_j n` on the frequencies, `v ↦ ± R_j^* v` on the coefficients. -/
def symmetries (rel : Bool) : (windowSymbol d).Symmetries d where
  R j := Reflection.count_of_involutive (flipAt j) (flipAt_involutive j)
  ρ j i := parSign rel • reflForm j i
  invol j i v := by
    simp only [_root_.smul_apply, _root_.map_smul, reflForm_reflForm, smul_smul,
      parSign_mul_self, one_smul]
  inner_ρ j i v w := by
    simp only [_root_.smul_apply, inner_smul_left, inner_smul_right, inner_reflForm, ← mul_assoc]
    rw [mul_comm (parSign rel), conj_parSign_mul_self, one_mul]
  symm j i i' n v := by
    change (deRham d).m i i' (Fourier.Torus.freq (flipAt j n)) (parSign rel • reflForm j i v) =
      parSign rel • reflForm j i' ((deRham d).m i i' (Fourier.Torus.freq n) v)
    rw [freq_flipAt, _root_.map_smul, deRham_reflForm]
  comm_σ j l n := flipAt_comm j l n
  comm_ρ j l i v := by
    simp only [_root_.smul_apply, _root_.map_smul, reflForm_comm j l, smul_smul]

variable (d) in
/-- The action of `(ℤ/2)ᵈ` on the torus de Rham window generated by the reflections. -/
abbrev action (rel : Bool) : (window d).Action (Multiplicative (d → ZMod 2)) :=
  (symmetries d rel).toAction

instance instCompleteSpaceFixed (rel : Bool) (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) :
    CompleteSpace ((action d rel).fixed i) :=
  ((action d rel).isClosed_fixed i).completeSpace_coe

variable (d) in
/-- **The de Rham complex of the cube** in a parity class (the method of images). -/
abbrev complex (rel : Bool) :
    HilbertComplex ℂ (ComplexShape.window (Fintype.card d + 1)) fun i => (action d rel).fixed i :=
  (action d rel).fixedComplex

variable (d) in
/-- **Relative boundary conditions** (tangential trace zero): `ω_s` odd in `x_j` for `j ∉ s`,
even for `j ∈ s`. -/
abbrev relative := complex d true

variable (d) in
/-- **Absolute boundary conditions** (normal trace zero): `ω_s` even in `x_j` for `j ∉ s`, odd
for `j ∈ s`. -/
abbrev absolute := complex d false

/-- **The parity classes, coefficientwise**: `u` is fixed iff `± R_j^* u(flip_j n) = u(n)` for all
`j` and `n`. -/
theorem mem_fixed_iff {rel : Bool} {i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)}
    {u : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))} :
    u ∈ (action d rel).fixed i ↔
      ∀ j n, parSign rel • reflForm j i (u (flipAt j n)) = u n := by
  rw [(symmetries d rel).mem_fixed_toAction]
  refine forall_congr' fun j => ⟨fun h n => ?_, fun h => Lp.ext_count fun n => ?_⟩
  · have e := Measure.ae_count_iff.1 (coeFn_symLp ((symmetries d rel).R j)
      ((symmetries d rel).ρ j i) u) n
    rw [h] at e
    exact e.symm
  · rw [Measure.ae_count_iff.1 (coeFn_symLp ((symmetries d rel).R j)
      ((symmetries d rel).ρ j i) u) n]
    exact h n

/-! ### Compactness, closed range, eigenbasis -/

/-- **The compactness property of the de Rham complex of the cube** in both parity classes, in
every degree (Rellich and Gaffney on cubes, in this model). [AFW2010], §4.3 -/
theorem hasCompactProperty (rel : Bool) : (complex d rel).HasCompactProperty :=
  (action d rel).hasCompactProperty_fixedComplex window_hasCompactProperty

/-- **Closed range in every degree.** -/
theorem closedRangeAt (rel : Bool) (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) :
    (complex d rel).ClosedRangeAt i :=
  (hasCompactProperty rel i).closedRangeAt

/-- Closed range of the adjoint complex in every degree. -/
theorem dual_closedRangeAt (rel : Bool) (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) :
    (complex d rel).dual.ClosedRangeAt i :=
  (hasCompactProperty rel i).dual_closedRangeAt

/-- Finite-dimensional harmonic forms in every degree. -/
theorem finiteDimensional_harmonic (rel : Bool) (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) :
    FiniteDimensional ℂ ((complex d rel).harmonic i) :=
  (hasCompactProperty rel i).finiteDimensional_harmonic

/-- The Poincaré inequality of the torus window, `‖u‖ ≤ (2π)⁻¹ ‖d u‖` on `D(d) ∩ N(d)ᗮ`. -/
theorem window_norm_le_of_mem_orthogonal {i j : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)}
    (u : ((window d).d i j).domain)
    (hu : (u : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) ∈ ((window d).d i j).kerᗮ) :
    ‖(u : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ)))‖ ≤
      (2 * Real.pi)⁻¹ * ‖(window d).d i j u‖ := by
  refine (windowSymbol d).norm_le_of_gap (Filter.Eventually.of_forall fun n => ?_) u hu
  by_cases hn : n = 0
  · subst hn
    intro v hv
    have h0 : (windowSymbol d).m i j 0 = 0 := by
      change (deRham d).m i j (Fourier.Torus.freq 0) = 0
      rw [Fourier.Torus.freq_zero, deRham_m_zero]
    rw [h0] at hv ⊢
    simp [eq_zero_of_mem_orthogonal_ker_zero hv]
  · exact gap _ _ (Fourier.Torus.two_pi_le_norm_freq hn)

/-- **The Poincaré inequality on the cube**, in both parity classes and every degree:
`‖u‖ ≤ (2π)⁻¹ ‖d u‖` for `u ∈ D(d) ∩ N(d)ᗮ`. -/
theorem norm_le_of_mem_orthogonal (rel : Bool) {i j : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)}
    (u : ((complex d rel).d i j).domain)
    (hu : (u : (action d rel).fixed i) ∈ ((complex d rel).d i j).kerᗮ) :
    ‖(u : (action d rel).fixed i)‖ ≤ (2 * Real.pi)⁻¹ * ‖(complex d rel).d i j u‖ :=
  (action d rel).reducingSubcomplex_fixed.norm_le_of_mem_orthogonal
    window_norm_le_of_mem_orthogonal u hu

/-- **A complete set of eigenvectors** for the Hodge wave group of the de Rham complex of the
cube, in both parity classes (compact resolvent). -/
theorem eigenDense (rel : Bool) : (complex d rel).waveGroup.EigenDense :=
  (action d rel).eigenDense_fixedComplex Torus.DeRham.window_eigenDense

/-! ### Harmonic forms -/

/-- **The harmonic forms of the torus window are the constant forms.** -/
theorem mem_window_harmonic_iff {i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)}
    {u : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))} :
    u ∈ (window d).harmonic i ↔ ∀ n, n ≠ 0 → u n = 0 := by
  rw [SymbolComplex.harmonic_toHilbertComplex, Operator.mem_fibreSub, Measure.ae_count_iff]
  refine forall_congr' fun n => ?_
  by_cases hn : n = 0
  · subst hn
    have h0 : ∀ a b, (windowSymbol d).m a b 0 = 0 := fun a b => by
      change (deRham d).m a b (Fourier.Torus.freq 0) = 0
      rw [Fourier.Torus.freq_zero, deRham_m_zero]
    simp [h0]
  · have hξ : ‖Fourier.Torus.freq n‖ ≠ 0 :=
      norm_ne_zero_iff.2 fun h => hn (Fourier.Torus.freq_eq_zero_iff.1 h)
    refine ⟨fun h _ => ?_, fun h => by rw [h hn]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _⟩
    obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := Submodule.mem_inf.1 h
    have hc := window_cartan i (Fourier.Torus.freq n) (u n)
    have e1 : (windowSymbol d).m i ((ComplexShape.window (Fintype.card d + 1)).next i) n (u n) = 0 :=
      LinearMap.mem_ker.1 h1
    have e2 : ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint
        ((windowSymbol d).m ((ComplexShape.window (Fintype.card d + 1)).prev i) i n) (u n) = 0 :=
      LinearMap.mem_ker.1 h2
    change ‖(deRham d).m i _ (Fourier.Torus.freq n) (u n)‖ ^ 2 +
      ‖ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint ((deRham d).m _ i (Fourier.Torus.freq n)) (u n)‖ ^ 2 = _ at hc
    change (deRham d).m i _ (Fourier.Torus.freq n) (u n) = 0 at e1
    change ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint ((deRham d).m _ i (Fourier.Torus.freq n)) (u n) = 0 at e2
    rw [e1, e2] at hc
    simp only [norm_zero, ne_eq, OfNat.ofNat_ne_zero, not_false_eq_true, zero_pow,
      add_zero] at hc
    have h3 := (mul_eq_zero.1 hc.symm).resolve_left (pow_ne_zero 2 hξ)
    exact norm_eq_zero.1 ((pow_eq_zero_iff two_ne_zero).1 h3)

/-- **The harmonic forms of the cube** are the fixed constant forms. -/
theorem mem_harmonic_iff {rel : Bool} {i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)} {x : (action d rel).fixed i} :
    x ∈ (complex d rel).harmonic i ↔
      ∀ n, n ≠ 0 → (x : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) n = 0 :=
  ((action d rel).mem_harmonic_fixedComplex_iff).trans mem_window_harmonic_iff

/-- The zero mode of a fixed form is fixed by every `± R_j^*`. -/
theorem parSign_reflForm_zero {rel : Bool} {i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)}
    (x : (action d rel).fixed i) (j : d) (t : {s : Finset d // (#s : ℤ) = (i : ℕ)}) :
    parSign rel * reflSign j t.1 *
        (x : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) 0 t =
      (x : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) 0 t := by
  have h := congrArg (fun v : Form ℂ d i => v t) (mem_fixed_iff.1 x.2 j 0)
  simp only [flipAt_zero, PiLp.smul_apply, reflForm_apply, smul_eq_mul] at h
  rw [mul_assoc]; exact h

/-- A harmonic form whose zero-mode coefficients vanish off `t₀` vanishes off `t₀`. -/
theorem harmonic_eq_bot_of {rel : Bool} {i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)}
    (h : ∀ t : {s : Finset d // (#s : ℤ) = (i : ℕ)}, ∃ j, parSign rel * reflSign j t.1 ≠ 1) :
    (complex d rel).harmonic i = ⊥ := by
  rw [eq_bot_iff]
  intro x hx
  rw [Submodule.mem_bot]
  refine Subtype.ext (Lp.ext_count fun n => ?_)
  rw [ZeroMemClass.coe_zero, coeFn_zero_count]
  by_cases hn : n = 0
  · subst hn
    ext t
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := h t
    have e := parSign_reflForm_zero x j t
    have : (x : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) 0 t = 0 := by
      by_contra hne
      exact hj (mul_right_cancel₀ hne (e.trans (one_mul _).symm))
    rw [this]; rfl
  · exact mem_harmonic_iff.1 hx n hn

/-- A harmonic space whose degree has a single index set `t₀` fixed by every `± R_j^*` is
one-dimensional, spanned by the constant form `dx_{t₀}`. -/
theorem finrank_harmonic_eq_one {rel : Bool} {i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)}
    (t₀ : {s : Finset d // (#s : ℤ) = (i : ℕ)}) (ht : ∀ t, t = t₀)
    (hs : ∀ j, parSign rel * reflSign j t₀.1 = 1) :
    Module.finrank ℂ ((complex d rel).harmonic i) = 1 := by
  set e₀ : Form ℂ d i := EuclideanSpace.single t₀ 1
  set v : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ)) := Torus.DeRham.const i e₀
  have hv : ∀ n, (v : (d → ℤ) → Form ℂ d i) n = if n = 0 then e₀ else 0 :=
    Torus.DeRham.const_apply i e₀
  have hfix : v ∈ (action d rel).fixed i := by
    refine mem_fixed_iff.2 fun j n => ?_
    rw [hv, hv]
    by_cases hn : n = 0
    · subst hn
      simp only [flipAt_zero, ite_true]
      ext t
      rw [ht t, PiLp.smul_apply, reflForm_apply, smul_eq_mul, ← mul_assoc, hs, one_mul]
    · have hn' : flipAt j n ≠ 0 := (flipAt_eq_zero_iff j).not.2 hn
      simp [hn, hn']
  set x : (action d rel).fixed i := ⟨v, hfix⟩
  have hx : x ∈ (complex d rel).harmonic i := mem_harmonic_iff.2 fun n hn => by
    change (v : (d → ℤ) → Form ℂ d i) n = 0
    simp [hv, hn]
  have hne : (⟨x, hx⟩ : (complex d rel).harmonic i) ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    have h1 : (v : (d → ℤ) → Form ℂ d i) 0 t₀ = 1 := by simp [hv, e₀]
    have h2 : v = 0 := by
      have := congrArg (fun y : (complex d rel).harmonic i =>
        ((y : (action d rel).fixed i) : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ)))) h0
      have h3 : x = 0 := by simpa using this
      exact congrArg Subtype.val h3
    rw [h2, coeFn_zero_count] at h1
    simp at h1
  refine (finrank_eq_one_iff_of_nonzero' _ hne).2 fun w => ?_
  refine ⟨((w : (action d rel).fixed i) : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ)))
    0 t₀, Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext (Lp.ext_count fun n => ?_))⟩
  simp only [Submodule.coe_smul]
  rw [coeFn_smul_count]
  change _ • (v : (d → ℤ) → Form ℂ d i) n = _
  rw [hv]
  by_cases hn : n = 0
  · subst hn
    simp only [ite_true]
    ext t
    rw [ht t]
    simp [e₀]
  · have hw0 : ((w : (action d rel).fixed i) : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2
        (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) n = 0 := mem_harmonic_iff.1 w.2 n hn
    rw [hw0]
    simp [hn]

/-- **Relative boundary conditions: no harmonic forms below the top degree.** -/
theorem relative_harmonic_eq_bot {i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)} (hi : (i : ℕ) ≠ Fintype.card d) :
    (relative d).harmonic i = ⊥ := by
  refine harmonic_eq_bot_of fun t => ?_
  have hne : t.1 ≠ Finset.univ := fun h => hi (by
    have := t.2; rw [h, Finset.card_univ] at this; exact_mod_cast this.symm)
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ : ∃ j, j ∉ t.1 := by
    by_contra h; push Not at h; exact hne (Finset.eq_univ_iff_forall.2 h)
  exact ⟨j, by simp [parSign, reflSign, hj]; norm_num⟩

/-- **Relative boundary conditions: the harmonic `n`-forms are one-dimensional**
(`ℌⁿ = span (dx_1 ∧ ⋯ ∧ dx_n)`, `Hⁿ(Q, ∂Q) ≅ ℂ`). -/
theorem finrank_relative_harmonic_top :
    Module.finrank ℂ ((relative d).harmonic (Fin.last (Fintype.card d))) = 1 := by
  refine finrank_harmonic_eq_one ⟨Finset.univ, by simp⟩
    (fun t => Subtype.ext (Finset.eq_univ_of_card _ (by
      have := t.2; simp only [Fin.val_last] at this; exact_mod_cast this))) fun j => ?_
  simp [parSign, reflSign]

/-- **Absolute boundary conditions: no harmonic forms above degree `0`.** -/
theorem absolute_harmonic_eq_bot {i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)} (hi : (i : ℕ) ≠ 0) :
    (absolute d).harmonic i = ⊥ := by
  refine harmonic_eq_bot_of fun t => ?_
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ : t.1.Nonempty := Finset.card_pos.1 (by have := t.2; omega)
  exact ⟨j, by simp [parSign, reflSign, hj]; norm_num⟩

/-- **Absolute boundary conditions: the harmonic `0`-forms are the constants**
(`H⁰(Q) ≅ ℂ`). -/
theorem finrank_absolute_harmonic_zero : Module.finrank ℂ ((absolute d).harmonic 0) = 1 := by
  refine finrank_harmonic_eq_one ⟨∅, by simp⟩
    (fun t => Subtype.ext (Finset.card_eq_zero.1 (by
      have := t.2; simp only [Fin.val_zero, Nat.cast_zero] at this; exact_mod_cast this))) fun j => ?_
  simp [parSign, reflSign]

/-- **Duality of the harmonic forms** (Poincaré–Lefschetz, numerically): the relative harmonic
`k`-forms and the absolute harmonic `k'`-forms, `k + k' = n`, have the same dimension. -/
theorem finrank_relative_harmonic_eq_absolute {k k' : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)}
    (hkk : (k : ℕ) + k' = Fintype.card d) :
    Module.finrank ℂ ((relative d).harmonic k) = Module.finrank ℂ ((absolute d).harmonic k') := by
  by_cases hk : (k : ℕ) = Fintype.card d
  · obtain rfl : k = Fin.last _ := Fin.ext hk
    obtain rfl : k' = 0 := Fin.ext (by simp at hkk ⊢; omega)
    exact finrank_relative_harmonic_top.trans finrank_absolute_harmonic_zero.symm
  · have h1 : Module.finrank ℂ ((relative d).harmonic k) = 0 := by
      rw [relative_harmonic_eq_bot hk]; exact finrank_bot ℂ _
    have h2 : Module.finrank ℂ ((absolute d).harmonic k') = 0 := by
      rw [absolute_harmonic_eq_bot (by omega)]; exact finrank_bot ℂ _
    rw [h1, h2]

/-- Duality of the harmonic forms, `k ↔ n - k` (`Fin.rev`). -/
theorem finrank_relative_harmonic_eq_absolute_rev (k : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) :
    Module.finrank ℂ ((relative d).harmonic k) = Module.finrank ℂ ((absolute d).harmonic k.rev) :=
  finrank_relative_harmonic_eq_absolute (by rw [Fin.val_rev]; have := k.isLt; omega)

/-! ### The Hodge star exchanges the two classes -/

section LpMap

variable {α : Type*} [MeasurableSpace α] [MeasurableSingletonClass α]
  {E F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E]
  [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℂ F]

/-- A fibre isometry `e : E ≃ₗᵢ F` acts pointwise on `ℓ²(α; E)`, `u ↦ e ∘ u`. -/
noncomputable def lpCongr (e : E ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] F) :
    Lp E 2 (Measure.count : Measure α) ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] Lp F 2 (Measure.count : Measure α) where
  toFun u := (e : E →L[ℂ] F).compLp u
  invFun w := (e.symm : F →L[ℂ] E).compLp w
  map_add' := ((e : E →L[ℂ] F).compLpₗ 2 (Measure.count : Measure α)).map_add
  map_smul' := ((e : E →L[ℂ] F).compLpₗ 2 (Measure.count : Measure α)).map_smul
  left_inv u := Lp.ext_count fun a => by
    rw [Measure.ae_count_iff.1 (ContinuousLinearMap.coeFn_compLp _ _) a,
      Measure.ae_count_iff.1 (ContinuousLinearMap.coeFn_compLp _ _) a]
    simp
  right_inv w := Lp.ext_count fun a => by
    rw [Measure.ae_count_iff.1 (ContinuousLinearMap.coeFn_compLp _ _) a,
      Measure.ae_count_iff.1 (ContinuousLinearMap.coeFn_compLp _ _) a]
    simp
  norm_map' u := by
    change ‖(e : E →L[ℂ] F).compLp u‖ = ‖u‖
    rw [Lp.norm_def, Lp.norm_def]
    refine congrArg ENNReal.toReal (eLpNorm_congr_norm_ae (Lp.aestronglyMeasurable _)
      (Lp.aestronglyMeasurable _) ?_)
    filter_upwards [ContinuousLinearMap.coeFn_compLp (e : E →L[ℂ] F) u] with a ha
    rw [ha]; exact e.norm_map _

omit [MeasurableSingletonClass α] in
theorem lpCongr_apply (e : E ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] F) (u : Lp E 2 (Measure.count : Measure α)) (a : α) :
    lpCongr e u a = e (u a) :=
  Measure.ae_count_iff.1 (ContinuousLinearMap.coeFn_compLp (e : E →L[ℂ] F) u) a

end LpMap

variable (d) in
/-- Complementation `s ↦ sᶜ` of the index sets of `k`-forms and `k'`-forms, `k + k' = n`. -/
def complIdx {k k' : ℤ} (h : k + k' = Fintype.card d) :
    {s : Finset d // (#s : ℤ) = k} ≃ {s : Finset d // (#s : ℤ) = k'} where
  toFun t := ⟨t.1ᶜ, by have := t.2; have := Finset.card_le_univ t.1; rw [Finset.card_compl]; omega⟩
  invFun t := ⟨t.1ᶜ, by have := t.2; have := Finset.card_le_univ t.1; rw [Finset.card_compl]; omega⟩
  left_inv t := Subtype.ext (compl_compl _)
  right_inv t := Subtype.ext (compl_compl _)

variable (d) in
/-- **The Hodge star up to sign**, `dx_s ↦ dx_{sᶜ}`, an isometry of `k`-forms onto `k'`-forms,
`k + k' = n`. -/
noncomputable def complForm {k k' : ℤ} (h : k + k' = Fintype.card d) :
    Form ℂ d k ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] Form ℂ d k' :=
  LinearIsometryEquiv.piLpCongrLeft 2 ℂ ℂ (complIdx d h)

theorem complForm_apply {k k' : ℤ} (h : k + k' = Fintype.card d) (v : Form ℂ d k)
    (t : {s : Finset d // (#s : ℤ) = k'}) : complForm d h v t = v ⟨t.1ᶜ, by
      have := t.2; have := Finset.card_le_univ t.1; rw [Finset.card_compl]; omega⟩ := by
  simp [complForm, LinearIsometryEquiv.piLpCongrLeft_apply, Equiv.piCongrLeft'_apply]
  rfl

theorem reflSign_compl (j : d) (s : Finset d) : reflSign j sᶜ = -reflSign j s := by
  unfold reflSign; by_cases hj : j ∈ s <;> simp [hj]

theorem reflForm_complForm {k k' : ℤ} (h : k + k' = Fintype.card d) (j : d) (v : Form ℂ d k) :
    reflForm j k' (complForm d h v) = -complForm d h (reflForm j k v) := by
  ext t
  simp only [reflForm_apply, complForm_apply, PiLp.neg_apply]
  have e := reflSign_compl j (t.1)ᶜ
  rw [compl_compl] at e
  rw [e]
  ring

theorem parSign_not (rel : Bool) : parSign (!rel) = -parSign rel := by
  cases rel <;> norm_num [parSign]

omit [LinearOrder d] in
theorem add_val_rev (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) :
    ((i : ℕ) : ℤ) + (i.rev : ℕ) = Fintype.card d := by
  rw [Fin.val_rev]; have := i.isLt; omega

variable (d) in
/-- The Hodge star up to sign, `u ↦ ⋆ ∘ u`, on the Fourier coefficients of the torus window,
from degree `i` to degree `n - i`. -/
noncomputable def starLp (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) :
    Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ)) ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ]
      Lp (Form ℂ d i.rev) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ)) :=
  lpCongr (complForm d (add_val_rev i))

theorem starLp_apply (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1))
    (u : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) (n : d → ℤ) :
    starLp d i u n = complForm d (add_val_rev i) (u n) :=
  lpCongr_apply _ u n

/-- **The Hodge star exchanges the parity classes**: `⋆ u` is absolute iff `u` is relative, and
conversely. -/
theorem starLp_mem_fixed_iff {rel : Bool} {i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)}
    {u : Lp (Form ℂ d i) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))} :
    starLp d i u ∈ (action d (!rel)).fixed i.rev ↔ u ∈ (action d rel).fixed i := by
  rw [mem_fixed_iff, mem_fixed_iff]
  refine forall_congr' fun j => forall_congr' fun n => ?_
  rw [starLp_apply, starLp_apply, reflForm_complForm, parSign_not, smul_neg, neg_smul, neg_neg,
    ← LinearIsometryEquiv.map_smul, (complForm d (add_val_rev i)).injective.eq_iff]

variable (d) in
/-- **The Hodge star (up to sign) as a unitary map between the parity classes**, from degree
`i` of one class to degree `n - i` of the other: relative `i`-forms onto absolute `(n - i)`-forms
(`rel = true`) and absolute onto relative (`rel = false`). -/
noncomputable def hodgeStar (rel : Bool) (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) :
    (action d rel).fixed i ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] (action d (!rel)).fixed i.rev where
  toFun x := ⟨starLp d i x, starLp_mem_fixed_iff.2 x.2⟩
  invFun y := ⟨(starLp d i).symm y, starLp_mem_fixed_iff.1 (by simp)⟩
  map_add' x y := Subtype.ext (map_add (starLp d i) _ _)
  map_smul' c x := Subtype.ext ((starLp d i).map_smul c _)
  left_inv x := Subtype.ext (by simp)
  right_inv y := Subtype.ext (by simp)
  norm_map' x := (starLp d i).norm_map x

theorem coe_hodgeStar (rel : Bool) (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) (x : (action d rel).fixed i) :
    (hodgeStar d rel i x : Lp (Form ℂ d i.rev) 2 (Measure.count : Measure (d → ℤ))) =
      starLp d i x := rfl

/-- **The Hodge star exchanges the harmonic forms of the two classes**, `k ↔ n - k`. -/
theorem hodgeStar_mem_harmonic_iff {rel : Bool} {i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)}
    {x : (action d rel).fixed i} :
    hodgeStar d rel i x ∈ (complex d (!rel)).harmonic i.rev ↔ x ∈ (complex d rel).harmonic i := by
  rw [mem_harmonic_iff, mem_harmonic_iff]
  refine forall_congr' fun n => imp_congr_right fun _ => ?_
  rw [coe_hodgeStar, starLp_apply, LinearIsometryEquiv.map_eq_zero_iff]

variable (d) in
/-- The Hodge star (up to sign) restricted to harmonic forms: a unitary isomorphism
`ℌᵏ ≅ ℌ*ⁿ⁻ᵏ` between the harmonic forms of the two classes. -/
noncomputable def harmonicHodgeStar (rel : Bool) (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) :
    (complex d rel).harmonic i ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] (complex d (!rel)).harmonic i.rev where
  toFun x := ⟨hodgeStar d rel i x, hodgeStar_mem_harmonic_iff.2 x.2⟩
  invFun y := ⟨(hodgeStar d rel i).symm y, hodgeStar_mem_harmonic_iff.1 (by simp)⟩
  map_add' x y := Subtype.ext (map_add (hodgeStar d rel i) _ _)
  map_smul' c x := Subtype.ext ((hodgeStar d rel i).map_smul c _)
  left_inv x := Subtype.ext (by simp)
  right_inv y := Subtype.ext (by simp)
  norm_map' x := (hodgeStar d rel i).norm_map x

/-- **Duality of the harmonic forms**, from the unitary `harmonicHodgeStar`: the harmonic
`k`-forms of one class and the harmonic `(n - k)`-forms of the other have the same dimension. -/
theorem finrank_harmonic_eq_rev (rel : Bool) (i : Fin (Fintype.card d + 1)) :
    Module.finrank ℂ ((complex d rel).harmonic i) =
      Module.finrank ℂ ((complex d (!rel)).harmonic i.rev) :=
  (harmonicHodgeStar d rel i).toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq

end Feec.Models.Cube.DeRham
